WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.076
Watch a packer for one minute.

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:06.738
Count how often they turn, stretch or walk.

00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:08.989
Most of that movement is avoidable.

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:14.042
When tape, film, cartons and labels are scattered, packing slows down,

00:00:14.042 --> 00:00:16.841
and mistakes in labels and weights creep in.

00:00:17.121 --> 00:00:21.072
With several packers sharing materials, people also queue and wait.

00:00:21.672 --> 00:00:25.209
A good packing station keeps every consumable within reach.

00:00:25.489 --> 00:00:28.200
Roll holders dispense film and bubble wrap.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.271
Shelf dividers keep cartons sorted by size.

00:00:31.551 --> 00:00:36.640
A label holder sits at hand, a power rail feeds the sealer, printer and scale,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.185
and a board shows packing instructions.

00:00:39.465 --> 00:00:44.432
Keep tape and cutters within half a metre of the packer, and spare rolls within one metre.

00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:50.545
Furnisys packing accessories fit Scitec and Pro benches, base cabinets and Link frames.

00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:56.624
A bearing maker runs eight identical packing stations this way, and a tooling company wraps,

00:00:56.624 --> 00:00:59.272
weighs and labels each die at one station.

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:01.832
Pack in one place, with one reach.

00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:03.911
What slows down your packing most?

00:01:04.191 --> 00:01:07.202
Comment below, and next, find the right working height.

00:01:07.802 --> 00:01:12.047
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

